#~ msgid "All"
#~ msgstr "Toos"

#~ msgid "In 1969, [Ken Thompson](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ken_Thompson) and [Dennis Ritchie](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dennis_Ritchie) started working on [UNIX](http://www.unix.org/what_is_unix/history_timeline.html). Initially written in assembler, it was soon rewritten in [C](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C_(programming_language)), a language created by Ritchie and considered high level."
#~ msgstr "En 1969, [Ken Thompson](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ken_Thompson) y [Dennis Ritchie](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dennis_Ritchie) comenzaron a trabayar n'[UNIX](http://www.unix.org/what_is_unix/history_timeline.html). Escritu nel aniciu n'ensamblador, pronto lu reescribieron en [C](https://ast.wikipedia.org/wiki/Llinguaxe_de_programaci%C3%B3n_C), un llingüaxe creáu por Ritchie y consideráu de nivel altu."

#~ msgid "Thompson & Ritchie"
#~ msgstr "Thompson y Ritchie"

#~ msgid "UNIX is born"
#~ msgstr "Naz UNIX"

#~ msgid "In 1979, [Bjarne Stroustrup](http://www.stroustrup.com/bio.html) started developing \"C with classes\", which would later become the [C++](http://www.softwarepreservation.org/projects/c_plus_plus/). In his opinion, it was the only language of the time that allowed to write programs that were at the same time efficient and elegant."
#~ msgstr "En 1979, [Bjarne Stroustrup](http://www.stroustrup.com/bio.html) comenzó'l desendolcu de «C con clases» que dempués diba convertise en [C ++](http://www.softwarepreservation.org/projects/c_plus_plus/). Na so opinión, yera l'únicu llingüaxe d'entós que permitía escribir programes que yeren eficientes y elegantes al empar."

#~ msgid "Bjarne Stroustrup"
#~ msgstr "Bjarne Stroustrup"

#~ msgid "C++ was created"
#~ msgstr "Creóse C++"

#~ msgid "In 1984, [Richard Stallman](https://stallman.org/biographies.html#serious) started developing [GNU](https://www.gnu.org/gnu/about-gnu.html) (GNU is Not Unix), a completely free operating system based on Unix, which was proprietary."
#~ msgstr "En 1984, [Richard Stallman](https://stallman.org/biographies.html#serious comenzó'l desendolcu de [GNU](https://www.gnu.org/gnu/about-gnu.html) (GNU in Not Unix «GNU nun ye Unix»), un sistema  operativu llibre dafechu basáu en Unix, que yera privativu."

#~ msgid "Richard Stallman"
#~ msgstr "Richard Stallman"

#~ msgid "The beginning of Free Software"
#~ msgstr "El comienzu del software llibre"

#~ msgid "In 1991, [Linus Torvalds](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linus_Torvalds) created the [Linux kernel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_kernel) based on [MINIX](http://www.minix3.org/), a version of Unix written by [Andrew Tanenbaum](http://www.cs.vu.nl/~ast/home/faq.html). The emergence of Linux has revolutionized the history of free software and helped to popularize it. See the [25 Years of Linux Kernel Development infographic](https://web.archive.org/web/20190628003733im_/https://www.linux.com/sites/lcom/files/styles/rendered_file/public/linux-kernel-development-infographic-2016.jpg?itok=DqVqiplt)."
#~ msgstr "En 1991, [Linus Torvalds](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linus_Torvalds) creó'l [kernel Linux](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_kernel) basáu en [MINIX](http://www.minix3.org/), una versión d'Unix escrita por [Andrew Tanenbaum](http://www.cs.vu.nl/~ast/home/faq.html). El xurdimientu de Linux revolucionó la historia del software llibre y ayudó a popularizalu. Mira la [infografía de los 25 años de desendolcu del kernel Linux](https://web.archive.org/web/20190628003733im_/https://www.linux.com/sites/lcom/files/styles/rendered_file/public/linux-kernel-development-infographic-2016.jpg?itok=DqVqiplt)."

#~ msgid "Linus Torvalds"
#~ msgstr "Linus Torvalds"

#~ msgid "The Linux Kernel"
#~ msgstr "El kernel Linux"

#~ msgid "In 1993, the first free distributions begin to emerge, based in [GNU and Linux](http://www.aboutlinux.info/2005/11/complete-concise-history-of-gnulinux.html). A [GNU/Linux distribution](http://futurist.se/gldt/) is usually formed by the Linux kernel, GNU tools and libraries, and more a collection of applications."
#~ msgstr "En 1993 xurdieron les primeres distribuciones llibres basaes en [GNU y Linux](http://www.aboutlinux.info/2005/11/complete-concise-history-of-gnulinux.html). Una [distribución GNU/Linux](http://futurist.se/gldt/) componse del kernel Linux, les ferramientes y biblioteques de GNU, y más aplicaciones."

#~ msgid "GNU & Tux"
#~ msgstr "GNU y Tux"

#~ msgid "The first distros are born"
#~ msgstr "Nacen les primeres distros"

#~ msgid "In 1995, the Norwegian company Troll Tech created the cross-platform framework [Qt](https://wiki.qt.io/About_Qt), with which KDE would be created in the following year. Qt became the basis of the main KDE technologies in these 20 years. Learn more about [Qt History](https://wiki.qt.io/Qt_History)."
#~ msgstr "En 1995, la compaña noruega Troll Tech creó'l framework multiplataforma [Qt](https://wiki.qt.io/About_Qt), col que se crearía KDE al añu siguiente. Qt convirtióse na base fundamental de les teunoloxíes de KDE nestos 20 años. Deprendi más tocante a la [historia de Qt](https://wiki.qt.io/Qt_History)."

#~ msgid "Qt logo"
#~ msgstr "Logotipu de Qt"

#~ msgid "Qt was created"
#~ msgstr "Creóse Qt"

#~ msgid "In 1996, [Matthias Ettrich](http://www.linuxjournal.com/article/6834) announced the creation of Kool Desktop Environment (KDE), a graphical interface for Unix systems, built with Qt and C ++ and designed for the end user. The name \"KDE\" was a pun on the graphic environment [CDE](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Desktop_Environment), which was proprietary at the time. Read [the original announcement](https://www.kde.org/announcements/announcement.php) of the KDE Project."
#~ msgstr "En 1996, [Matthias Ettrich](http://www.linuxjournal.com/article/6834) anunció la creación del Kool Desktop Environment (KDE), una interfaz gráfica d'usuariu pa sistemes Unix, fecha con Qt y C ++, y diseñada pal usuariu final. El nome «KDE» yera un xuegu de pallabres del entornu gráficu [CDE](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Desktop_Environment), que yera privativu daquella. Llei [l'anunciu orixinal](https://www.kde.org/announcements/announcement.php) del proyeutu KDE."

#~ msgid "Matthias Ettrich"
#~ msgstr "Matthias Ettrich"

#~ msgid "KDE was announced"
#~ msgstr "Anuncióse KDE"

#~ msgid "In 1997, about 15 KDE developers met in Arnsberg, Germany, to work on the project and discuss its future. This event became known as [KDE One](https://community.kde.org/KDE_Project_History/KDE_One_(Developer_Meeting))."
#~ msgstr "En 1997, alredor de 15 desendolcadores de KDE aconceyaron n'Arnsberg (Alemaña) pa trabayar nel proyeutu y aldericar el so futuru. Esti eventu conocióse como [KDE One](https://community.kde.org/KDE_Project_History/KDE_One_(Developer_Meeting))."

#~ msgid "Cornelius Schumacher's Archive"
#~ msgstr "L'archivu de Cornelius Schumacher"

#~ msgid "KDE One Conference"
#~ msgstr "Conferencia KDE One"

#~ msgid "The beta 1 version of KDE was [released](https://www.kde.org/announcements/beta1announce.php) exactly 12 months after the project announcement. The release text emphasized that KDE was not a window manager, but an integrated environment in which the window manager was just another part."
#~ msgstr "La versión beta 1 de KDE [llanzóse](https://www.kde.org/announcements/beta1announce.php) puramente 12 meses dempués del anunciu del proyeutu. El testu del llanzamientu enfatizaba que KDE nun yera un xestor de ventanes, sinón un entornu integráu nel que'l xestor de ventanes yera namás otru componente."

#~ msgid "KDE Beta 1 Screenshot"
#~ msgstr "Captura de pantalla de KDE Beta 1"

#~ msgid "KDE Beta 1"
#~ msgstr "KDE Beta 1"

